## Why This Is Asked
Tests familiarity with Android architecture components (Room, Flow/LiveData, ViewModel, RecyclerView) and basic lifecycle handling. It also checks state management across rotations with minimal boilerplate.

## Key Concepts
- Room: Entity, DAO, and Database wiring
- Flow or LiveData for data observation
- ViewModel for lifecycle-aware state
- RecyclerView with DiffUtil for efficient updates
- Threading: Dispatchers.IO for DB ops

## Code Example
```kotlin
@Entity
data class Note(
  @PrimaryKey(autoGenerate = true) val id: Long = 0,
  val content: String,
  val timestamp: Long
)
@Dao
interface NoteDao {
  @Insert
  suspend fun insert(note: Note)
  @Query("SELECT * FROM Note ORDER BY timestamp DESC")
  fun getAll(): Flow<List<Note>>
  @Delete
  suspend fun delete(note: Note)
}
@Database(entities = [Note::class], version = 1)
abstract class NoteDatabase : RoomDatabase() {
  abstract fun noteDao(): NoteDao
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the Room migrations and data integrity?
- How would you handle large datasets (pagination, DiffUtil) and offline-first syncing considerations?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design an offline-first Android architecture using modern components like Jetpack Compose, Room, and WorkManager. It tests understanding of manifest-driven data flows and background synchronization suitable for beginners.

## Key Concepts

- MVVM architecture with Repository pattern
- Room database for local caching
- WorkManager for background synchronization
- Network constraints and offline-first design
- Jetpack Compose for UI rendering

## Code Example

```kotlin
data class Article(
    val id: String,
    val section: String,
    val title: String,
    val body: String,
    val updatedAt: Long
)

data class SectionManifest(
    val section: String,
    val endpoint: String
)

@Dao
interface ArticleDao {
    @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)
    suspend fun insertOrUpdate(article: Article)

    @Query("SELECT * FROM articles WHERE section = :section")
    fun getBySection(section: String): Flow<List<Article>>

    @Query("DELETE FROM articles WHERE section = :section")
    suspend fun clearSection(section: String)
}

class SyncWorker(
    context: Context,
    params: WorkerParameters
) : CoroutineWorker(context, params) {

    override suspend fun doWork(): Result {
        return try {
            // Fetch manifest and sync articles
            Result.success()
        } catch (e: Exception) {
            Result.retry()
        }
    }
}

val constraints = Constraints.Builder()
    .setRequiredNetworkType(NetworkType.UNMETERED)
    .setRequiresBatteryNotLow(true)
    .build()

val syncRequest = OneTimeWorkRequestBuilder<SyncWorker>()
    .setConstraints(constraints)
    .setBackoffCriteria(
        BackoffPolicy.EXPONENTIAL,
        30,
        TimeUnit.SECONDS
    )
    .build()
```
